# Modular & Reusable Code

## Hard limits

- **Max 300 lines per file.** If a file approaches 300 lines, split it before adding more.
- Write only what is needed for the current feature. No speculative helpers, unused props, dead comments, or over-abstraction.

## Modularity

- One clear responsibility per file (route, model, schema, UI component, hook, util).
- Prefer small modules over large “god” files.
- Split by layer: `routes` / `services` / `models` / `schemas` (server); `components` / `hooks` / `lib` (client).
- Extract shared logic into reusable modules instead of duplicating.

## Reuse first

- Before writing new code, check existing modules for something to reuse or extend.
- Shared UI → components; shared logic → hooks/utils; shared API types → shared schemas or types.
- Do not copy-paste blocks across files — extract and import.

## Keep it lean

- No wrappers that only pass through without adding value.
- No premature abstractions for one-time use.
- Prefer composition over deep inheritance or mega config objects.

## When splitting a file

```text
# ❌ growing into one big file
app/main.py          # routes + models + schemas + db all together

# ✅ split by concern
app/models/item.py
app/schemas/item.py
app/routers/items.py
app/services/items.py
```
